 it doesn't  sound like it would be Donald Trump's  politics now the back story about the  straws specifically is that the reason  straws have gotten so much attention is  that every day 500 million of these  plastic straws are used once  and they're thrown away because they're  small people often don't even put them  in trash cans so that they contribute a  lot to Street trash they get into  waterways it's terrible for animals and  they're not recyclable anyway in most  cases because of their small size and  they contain such little plastic so they  wreak havoc so that part makes sense  that's why straws have become a thing  there's been a movement to replace Pat  plastic straws either by having people  carry around their own reusable metal  straw to only give customers straws when  they've asked for them instead of  bringing them to everybody there are  some alternative straws made of like  paper and bamboo and different things  every one I've tried is truly terrible  some coffee shops I go to have switched  to these for ice drinks and they just  fall apart into mush within 10 minutes  so it's true that while the straws  aren't a lot of plastic the things Trump  is mentioning often are paper and the  large plastic items are recyclable so he  just doesn't get why people are even  talking about straws okay the really  important message here is no matter what  we as individuals do in terms of  consumer choices like these if we don't  have big picture wholesale change to  pollution resource usage and energy  usage this stuff is a drop in the bucket  and that's why all of these consumer  movements are fine to the extent that  they'll inform people hopefully they  will impact human behavior in some way  that makes a small change but Trump is  sort of getting at the idea that listen  we're not going to solve the climate  crisis climate crisis that is with  straws we need to be thinking way bigger  the problem is Trump's against most of  those way bigger picture changes that  need to be made he's trying to  revitalize an industry that should be  allowed to die both because it's failing  and it's terrible for the environment  the coal mining industry just as one  example from producing benefits or  trying to reduce financial benefits on  electric cars he is completely right  that if we have this myopic focus on  straws we're missing the big a bigger  picture he just doesn't understand how  we're missing the big a bigger picture  and he's against most of the bigger  picture changes that would need to be  made if we even want to look just at  like landfills right  if you just look at solid waste  landfills it's obviously mostly not  straws or even items for eating food  it's electronics products it's wood and  large industrial plastics if we zoom out  and look at the bigger picture of solid  waste beyond just consumer we're talking  about industry and manufacturing and  construction that are generating just  untold amounts of waste way bigger than  straws we zoom out a little more and you  realize if we really want to fix this  issue we've got to look at energy usage  and then figure out where is energy  usage coming from and this dwarfs the  straw issue so my point is not laugh at  the plastic straw people or laugh at  Trump for what he said the plastic straw  people have a specific cause it's a  logical one Trump seems to be  identifying that the straw issue is not  the be-all end-all the bring your groan  on grocery bag movement it's a good  movement but what we have to realize is  that we have to be thinking way way  bigger than these retail level consumer  choices which are important but if we  want to make real change happen and this  is why lots of corporations end up  getting behind these movements we need  to look at industry and we need to look  at transportation big picture and we  need to look at energy this is why a lot  of big corporations will say oh yeah  we're fully behind the plastic straw  thing going to paper or only bringing  straws when people ask for them they are  appearing to be part of the solution  while the real problem which is the much  broader use of energy transportation  fossil fuels that these huge  corporations contribute to that gets  ignored every time the attention gets  put on straw so Trump is right straws  are not the solution but he's against  most of the solutions that really would  make a big impact
 

